  "articleBody": "Custom wall paneling and decorative ceiling molding require tight tolerances. Small oversights during planning or installation can ruin the visual balance of an entire room. Keep an eye out for these frequent pitfalls:\n\n- Mismatched room scale: Selecting molding that is too heavy overwhelms low ceilings, while profiles that are too thin get lost in large rooms.\n- Overlooking wall irregularities: Fastening molding against unprepped, uneven drywall pulls joints apart. Walls must be checked and smoothed prior to install.\n- Inadequate fastening methods: Relying solely on finish nails without adhesive or solid wood blocking behind crown molding leads to sagging over time.\n- Forgetting natural wood movement: Failing to allow for temperature and humidity shifts causes custom wood joints to open during seasonal transitions.\n- Guessing corner angles: Few room corners are exactly 90 degrees. Cutting without measuring field angles leads to sloppy seams.\n- Leaving insufficient waste allowance: Custom milling requires extra material for pattern matching and returns; falling short causes severe job delays.\n\nWhat to Prepare Before You Start\nReview layout markings directly on the walls, confirm that backing or studs are located, and ensure all design profiles are scaled to your room's ceiling height before cutting.\n\nFor precision custom molding installed with care, call Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866.",
